189
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:14,340
The tool has collected information on whether the modules were tested before.

190
00:31:14,340 --> 00:31:30,280
At the same time, I will also check whether they have been tested in recent years.

191
00:31:40,280 --> 00:31:50,620
I have also created a formula for this, so I will paste the formula here.

192
00:31:53,620 --> 00:32:03,330
My formula will check against the tested database file and the task assignment file.

192
00:32:15,620 --> 00:32:18,330
This file right here.

193
00:32:27,330 --> 00:32:39,130
Here, I will check whether the module has already been tested using Cantata, GTest, or ASCET.

194
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:57,670
For tested modules, the formula returns the latest test environment.

195
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:59,605
If it is a C module, it will be tested using Cantata or GTest.

196
00:32:59,605 --> 00:33:09,540
If it is an ASW or ESP module, it will be tested using ASCET.

197
00:33:10,040 --> 00:33:18,590
The MT_Needed column is used to show whether the module has already been tested.

198
00:33:18,590 --> 00:33:31,640
If it has been tested, it will be mapped as Delta, and the effort for Delta will also be calculated.

199
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:46,640
I will apply the formula to all items here.

200
00:34:46,640 --> 00:34:54,230
Now I have checked all the information completely.

201
00:34:54,230 --> 00:35:01,745
If a module has not been tested, it will be new in this MT_Needed column.

202
00:35:01,745 --> 00:35:04,002
However, this test has already been tested.

203
00:35:04,002 --> 00:35:08,260
So my tested database file has been updated accordingly.

204
00:35:08,260 --> 00:35:17,080
Therefore, most modules in the MT_Needed column are Delta.

205
00:35:17,080 --> 00:35:22,690
Next, I will calculate the effort based on ELOC,

206
00:35:22,690 --> 00:35:26,995
in order to calculate the total effort for that module.

207
00:35:26,995 --> 00:35:38,300
The calculation is based on ELOC, Delta or New status, and test environment.

208
00:35:38,300 --> 00:35:51,233
To calculate this quickly, I have already written a formula and pasted it here.

209
00:35:55,233 --> 00:36:00,167
If I mark it as Valid, a C module will be counted as 0.1.

210
00:36:00,167 --> 00:36:04,100
The test environment will also be checked.

211
00:36:04,100 --> 00:36:08,360
If that C module is tested using GTest, it will use a different ELOC calculation.

212
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:13,035
If it is tested using Cantata, it will be calculated based on another ELOC.

213
00:36:13,035 --> 00:36:15,510
The same applies to ASCET.

214
00:36:15,510 --> 00:36:21,145
If it is EXP, it will be calculated using the ASCET formula.

215
00:36:26,145 --> 00:36:38,780
Here, it is Delta, so the total effort will be this value multiplied by 0.4.

216
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:49,840
Because the minimum effort for one module is 0.6, my formula gives 0.6 here.

217
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:56,360
I will apply this formula to all items here.

218
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:13,100
Earlier, I had not calculated effort for some modules.

219
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:18,840
So I will check again.
  
220
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:36,840
Select undefined

221
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:54,410
